CREATED:20260507T171850Z
DESCRIPTION:When we think of the Gospel\, or the "Good News\," we might th
 ink of Jesus in the book of Mark\, preaching throughout Galilee: "Repent 
 and believe the good news..." In some Christian traditions\, the Gospel i
 s simplified to a bare-bones message: "Jesus died for your sins." But the
 re is much depth\, beauty\, and richness in the vision of the Good News t
 hat Isaiah shares in chapters 52-58 of his prophecy. Join us for four wee
 ks in June as we dig into these passages and answer the question: "What i
 s the Gospel?"\n \nThe study will take place on Tuesday evenings from 7:0
 0-8:30 on June 9\, 16\, 23\, and 30 at Epworth United Methodist Church\, 
 3002 Hope Valley Road\, Durham. Email Mindy Erdmann at mindy.erdmann@duke
 .edu with questions.
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260507T171850Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260609T190000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260507T171850Z
LOCATION;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf6e-00000000:None
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:WHAT IS THE GOSPEL? A Four Week Study in Isaiah
